  partId: main_engine
  displayName: Orbital Manoeuvring System Engine
  shortName: Main Engine
  zone: 2
  order: 80
  keySpec: "AJ10-190  \xB7  25.7 kN thrust  \xB7  Isp 316 s"
  summary: The main engine, used for major trajectory changes including lunar orbit
    insertion and the Trans-Earth Injection burn home. The Artemis I engine had previously
    flown on nineteen Space Shuttle missions.
  whyItMatters: "It burns hypergolic propellants \u2014 monomethylhydrazine and nitrogen
    tetroxide \u2014 which ignite the instant they touch. There is no ignition system,
    because there is no ignition system to fail. Reliability beats performance when
    the engine must relight days from any help."
  narration: {fileID: 0}
